{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210692,"nonce":"iJf6FVPVzx1J1dqjaQWSTaUEGpA=","title":"wasm JIT: values held in wasm locals across a Call are invisible to GC","message":"wasm tier-up roots receiver + args inside wren_call_1 (runtime side, \"step 4a\"), but src/codegen/wasm.rs still emits no root push/restore around Call sites. Any value a JIT'd wasm function keeps in a local across a Call (a MakeList result, a GetField result, a previous Call's object result) can be reclaimed if the callee triggers GC. The wasm JIT has no stack maps; the GC only walks JIT_ROOTS_STORE.\n\nThis was dormant while mir_needs_unsupported_helpers rejected every allocating MIR shape. wasm/src/tier_up.rs has since relaxed that gate (Call arities 1..=4, MakeClosure up to 4 captures, inline upvalue access, make_list helpers), so the gap is now live.\n\n1. Allocate call_snap_local (i32) in scan_locals next to call_slot_local.\n2. Register imports when any Call exists: wren_jit_roots_snapshot_len() -\u003e i32, wren_jit_root_push(i64), wren_jit_roots_restore_len(i32). The wasm-bindgen exports already exist in wasm/src/tier_up.rs.\n3. In emit_instruction for Call: snapshot len, push receiver + each arg + every live local that holds a possibly-heap value, do the call, then restore len. Reload pushed locals from the root store after the call if the GC can move them.\n4. Cost is ~3 cross-instance hops per Call; measure fib(20) before and after.","files":null}]}